{
  "dom_id": "step-q60472",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "A wooden slat is $3\\,\\text{ft}$ long. Eddie needs to cut a piece that's $\\frac{5}{8}$ the length of the slat. How long is the piece he has to cut?",
  "worked_solution": "To find the length of the piece that Eddie has to cut, we have to multiply $3$ by $\\frac{5}{8}.$  \n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}\\times 3=\\frac{5\\times 3}{8}=\\frac{15}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{15}{8}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n15÷8=1\\,\\text{R}\\,7=1\\,\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nSo, Eddie has to cut a piece $1\\,\\frac{7}{8}\\,\\text{ft}$ long.",
